parts.text:
; x = *q`). Can the compiler propagate `*p`'s constant `10` to `*q`, or reorder a store to `*p` past a load from `*q`? Only if it knows whether $p$ and $q$ **alias** (point to overlapping memory locations):
* **Must-Alias:** $p$ and $q$ are guaranteed to point to the exact same memory address at runtime (enables Store-to-Load Forwarding).
* **May-Alias:** $p$ and $q$ *might* point to overlapping addresses (blocks reordering and dead-store elimination).
* **No-Alias:** $p$ and $q$ are guaranteed never to overlap (enables reordering, LICM of loads/stores, and vectorization).

Two classic flow-insensitive, context-insensitive pointer analysis algorithms compute global Points-To sets $\text{Pts}(p)$ (the set of abstract allocation sites that pointer $p$ may point to):

1. **Andersen's Inclusion-Based Analysis:** Models pointer assignments as subset constraints ($\subseteq$) solved via transitive closure in $O(N^3)$ worst-case time:
   * Address-of (`p = &a`): $\{a\} \subseteq \text{Pts}(p)$
   * Copy (`p = q`): $\text{Pts}(q) \subseteq \text{Pts}(p)$
   * Load (`p = *q`): $\forall x \in \text{Pts}(q),\; \text{Pts}(x) \subseteq \text{Pts}(p)$
   * Store (`*p = q`): $\forall x \in \text{Pts}(p),\; \text{Pts}(q) \subseteq \text{Pts}(x)$
2. **Steensgaard's Unification-Based Analysis:** Replaces subset constraints ($\subseteq$) with bidirectional equality constraints ($=$), merging points-to sets via an almost-linear $O(N \alpha(N))$ Union-Find data structure. It is much faster on massive codebases but less precise than Andersen's because assigning `p = q` merges the points-to equivalence classes of $p$ and $q$ in both directions.
3. **Type-Based Alias Analysis (TBAA):** Exploits source-language strict aliasing rules (e.g., in C/C++, an `int*` and a `float*` are assumed not to alias).

### 7.5 Concrete Walkthrough: Optimizing the Baseline SSA IR

Let us apply three optimization passes to our baseline SSA IR from Section 5.7.4:
1. **Peephole / Algebraic Strength Reduction on Modulo:** In `BB2`, `t1 = i1 % 2; t2 = t1 == 0` tests whether positive integer `i1` is even. Because $i_1 \ge 1$ is strictly positive, $i_1 \bmod 2$ is equivalent to a single-cycle bitwise AND: `t1 = i1 & 1`!
2. **Induction Variable Strength Reduction (IVSR):** As derived in Section 7.3, we replace `t3 = i1 * scale0` inside `BB3` with a strength-reduced derived induction variable `k` incremented by `scale0` in `BB5`.
3. **Copy Propagation & Dead Code Elimination:** Substituting `k1` directly into `sum2 = sum1 + k1` makes temporary `t3` dead, so DCE deletes `t3`.

**Optimized SSA IR for `compute(n, scale)`:**
```
BB0 (Preheader / Entry):
    sum0 = 0
    i0   = 1
    k0   = scale0                        // IVSR initialization: 1 * scale0
    jmp BB1

BB1 (Loop Header):
    sum1 = phi(BB0: sum0, BB5: sum4)
    i1   = phi(BB0: i0,   BB5: i2)
    k1   = phi(BB0: k0,   BB5: k2)       // IVSR phi node
    t0   = i1 <= n0
    br t0, BB2, BB6

BB2 (Loop Body - Bitwise Even Check):
    t1   = i1 & 1                        // Strength-reduced from (i1 % 2)
    t2   = t1 == 0
    br t2, BB3, BB4

BB3 (Then Branch):
    sum2 = sum1 + k1                     // Multiplication eliminated!
    jmp BB5

BB4 (Else Branch):
    sum3 = sum1 + i1
    jmp BB5

BB5 (If Join & Latch):
    sum4 = phi(BB3: sum2, BB4: sum3)
    i2   = i1 + 1
    k2   = k1 + scale0                   // IVSR additive step
    jmp BB1

BB6 (Exit):
    ret sum1
```

### 7.6 Production SSA Optimizer (SCCP + DCE) in C++

Below is a self-contained, working C++ implementation of an SSA IR representation along with **Sparse Conditional Constant Propagation (SCCP)** and **Dead Code Elimination (DCE)**.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <unordered_set>
#include <queue>
#include <string>
#include <utility>

enum class IROp {
    Const, Add, Sub, Mul, BitAnd, CmpEq, CmpLe, Phi, BrCond, Jump, Ret
};

struct PhiIncoming {
    int pred_bb;
    int ssa_reg;
};

struct IRInst {
    IROp op;
    int dst = -1;              // SSA destination register (-1 if none)
    int src1 = -1;             // First SSA operand
    int src2 = -1;             // Second SSA operand
    int64_t imm = 0;           // Constant immediate (for IROp::Const)
    std::vector<PhiIncoming> phi_args;
    int target_true = -1;      // For BrCond and Jump
    int target_false = -1;     // For BrCond
};

struct BasicBlock {
    int id;
    std::vector<IRInst> insts;
    std::vector<int> preds;
    std::vector<int> succs;
};

struct CFGFunction {
    std::vector<BasicBlock> blocks;
};

// --- Lattice for SCCP ---
enum class LatticeKind { Top, Constant, Bottom };

struct LatticeVal {
    LatticeKind kind = LatticeKind::Top;
    int64_t value = 0;

    bool operator==(const LatticeVal& o) const {
        if (kind != o.kind) return false;
        return kind != LatticeKind::Constant || value == o.value;
    }
    bool operator!=(const LatticeVal& o) const { return !(*this == o); }
};

static LatticeVal meet(LatticeVal a, LatticeVal b) {
    if (a.kind == LatticeKind::Top) return b;
    if (b.kind == LatticeKind::Top) return a;
    if (a.kind == LatticeKind::Bottom || b.kind == LatticeKind::Bottom) {
        return {LatticeKind::Bottom, 0};
    }
    if (a.value == b.value) return a;
    return {LatticeKind::Bottom, 0};
}

class SCCPOptimizer {
public:
    explicit SCCPOptimizer(CFGFunction& fn) : fn_(fn) {}

    void run_sccp_and_dce() {
        build_use_chains();

        // Initialize CFG worklist with entry block (BB 0)
        mark_edge_executable(-1, 0);

        while (!cfg_worklist_.empty() || !ssa_worklist_.empty()) {
            while (!cfg_worklist_.empty()) {
                auto [pred, succ] = cfg_worklist_.front();
                cfg_worklist_.pop();
                BasicBlock& bb = fn_.blocks[succ];

                // Evaluate all Phi nodes in succ
                for (const auto& inst : bb.insts) {
                    if (inst.op == IROp::Phi) {
                        visit_inst(succ, inst);
                    }
                }
                // If this is the first time visiting succ, evaluate all instructions
                if (visited_blocks_.insert(succ).second) {
                    for (const auto& inst : bb.insts) {
                        if (inst.op != IROp::Phi) {
                            visit_inst(succ, inst);
                        }
                    }
                }
            }

            while (!ssa_worklist_.empty()) {
                auto [bb_id, inst_idx] = ssa_worklist_.front();
                ssa_worklist_.pop();
                if (visited_blocks_.count(bb_id)) {
                    visit_inst(bb_id, fn_.blocks[bb_id].insts[inst_idx]);
                }
            }
        }

        // Rewrite constant instructions into IROp::Const
        for (auto& bb : fn_.blocks) {
            for (auto& inst : bb.insts) {
                if (inst.dst != -1 && inst.op != IROp::Const) {
                    auto it = values_.find(inst.dst);
                    if (it != values_.end() && it->second.kind == LatticeKind::Constant) {
                        inst.op = IROp::Const;
                        inst.imm = it->second.value;
                        inst.src1 = -1;
                        inst.src2 = -1;
                        inst.phi_args.clear();
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        run_dead_code_elimination();
    }

    LatticeVal get_val(int reg) const {
        auto it = values_.find(reg);
        return (it != values_.end()) ? it->second : LatticeVal{LatticeKind::Top, 0};
    }

    void mark_param_overdefined(int reg) {
        values_[reg] = {LatticeKind::Bottom, 0};
    }

private:
    CFGFunction& fn_;
    std::unordered_map<int, LatticeVal> values_;
    std::unordered_map<int, std::vector<std::pair<int, size_t>>> ssa_uses_; // reg -> [(bb, inst_idx)]
    std::unordered_set<uint64_t> executable_edges_;
    std::unordered_set<int> visited_blocks_;
    std::queue<std::pair<int, int>> cfg_worklist_;
    std::queue<std::pair<int, size_t>> ssa_worklist_;

    static uint64_t edge_key(int u, int v) {
        return (static_cast<uint64_t>(static_cast<uint32_t>(u)) << 32) |
                static_cast<uint32_t>(v);
    }

    bool is_edge_executable(int u, int v) const {
        return executable_edges_.count(edge_key(u, v)) > 0;
    }

    void mark_edge_executable(int u, int v) {
        if (executable_edges_.insert(edge_key(u, v)).second) {
            cfg_worklist_.push({u, v});
        }
    }

    void build_use_chains() {
        ssa_uses_.clear();
        for (const auto& bb : fn_.blocks) {
            for (size_t i = 0; i < bb.insts.size(); ++i) {
                const auto& inst = bb.insts[i];
                if (inst.src1 != -1) ssa_uses_[inst.src1].push_back({bb.id, i});
                if (inst.src2 != -1) ssa_uses_[inst.src2].push_back({bb.id, i});
                for (const auto& pa : inst.phi_args) {
                    ssa_uses_[pa.ssa_reg].push_back({bb.id, i});
                }
            }
        }
    }

    void update_val(int reg, LatticeVal new_val) {
        LatticeVal old_val = get_val(reg);
        LatticeVal merged = meet(old_val, new_val);
        if (merged != old_val) {
            values_[reg] = merged;
            for (const auto& use : ssa_uses_[reg]) {
                ssa_worklist_.push(use);
            }
        }
    }

    void visit_inst(int bb_id, const IRInst& inst) {
        switch (inst.op) {
            case IROp::Const:
                update_val(inst.dst, {LatticeKind::Constant, inst.imm});
                break;
            case IROp::Phi: {
                LatticeVal acc{LatticeKind::Top, 0};
                for (const auto& pa : inst.phi_args) {
                    if (is_edge_executable(pa.pred_bb, bb_id)) {
                        acc = meet(acc, get_val(pa.ssa_reg));
                    }
                }
                update_val(inst.dst, acc);
                break;
            }
            case IROp::Add:
            case IROp::Sub:
            case IROp::Mul:
            case IROp::BitAnd:
            case IROp::CmpEq:
            case IROp::CmpLe: {
                LatticeVal v1 = get_val(inst.src1);
                LatticeVal v2 = get_val(inst.src2);
                if (v1.kind == LatticeKind::Constant && v2.kind == LatticeKind::Constant) {
                    int64_t res = 0;
                    if (inst.op == IROp::Add)    res = v1.value + v2.value;
                    if (inst.op == IROp::Sub)    res = v1.value - v2.value;
                    if (inst.op == IROp::Mul)    res = v1.value * v2.value;
                    if (inst.op == IROp::BitAnd) res = v1.value & v2.value;
                    if (inst.op == IROp::CmpEq)  res = (v1.value == v2.value) ? 1 : 0;
                    if (inst.op == IROp::CmpLe)  res = (v1.value <= v2.value) ? 1 : 0;
                    update_val(inst.dst, {LatticeKind::Constant, res});
                } else if (v1.kind == LatticeKind::Bottom || v2.kind == LatticeKind::Bottom) {
                    update_val(inst.dst, {LatticeKind::Bottom, 0});
                }
                break;
            }
            case IROp::Jump:
                mark_edge_executable(bb_id, inst.target_true);
                break;
            case IROp::BrCond: {
                LatticeVal cond = get_val(inst.src1);
                if (cond.kind == LatticeKind::Bottom) {
                    mark_edge_executable(bb_id, inst.target_true);
                    mark_edge_executable(bb_id, inst.target_false);
                } else if (cond.kind == LatticeKind::Constant) {
                    if (cond.value != 0) mark_edge_executable(bb_id, inst.target_true);
                    else                 mark_edge_executable(bb_id, inst.target_false);
                }
                break;
            }
            case IROp::Ret:
                break;
        }
    }

    // Worklist-based SSA Dead Code Elimination
    void run_dead_code_elimination() {
        bool changed = true;
        while (changed) {
            changed = false;
            std::unordered_set<int> used_regs;
            for (const auto& bb : fn_.blocks) {
                for (const auto& inst : bb.insts) {
                    if (inst.src1 != -1) used_regs.insert(inst.src1);
                    if (inst.src2 != -1) used_regs.insert(inst.src2);
                    for (const auto& pa : inst.phi_args) {
                        used_regs.insert(pa.ssa_reg);
                    }
                }
            }
            for (auto& bb : fn_.blocks) {
                auto it = bb.insts.begin();
                while (it != bb.insts.end()) {
                    if (it->dst != -1 && used_regs.count(it->dst) == 0) {
                        it = bb.insts.erase(it);
                        changed = true;
                    } else {
                        ++it;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
};
```

